{"html":"<p>Most Rust tutorials end at \"hello, world\". This project ends at a binary you can\n<code>cargo install</code> and use on a real 2 GB log file, with a benchmark that proves it.</p>\n<p><strong>What it is:</strong> <code>lens &#x3C;pattern> &#x3C;path></code> — recursive, parallel, gitignore-aware log\nsearch with coloured output, JSON mode and a <code>--top</code> summary of the noisiest paths.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-you-learn\">What you learn</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Skill</th>\n<th>Where it comes from</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Ownership across threads</td>\n<td><code>Arc</code>, <code>Send</code>, scoped threads</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Zero-copy parsing</td>\n<td><code>&#x26;str</code> slices, <code>memchr</code>, avoiding <code>String</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CLI ergonomics</td>\n<td><code>clap</code> derive, exit codes, stdin</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Real performance work</td>\n<td><code>perf</code>, criterion, allocation counting</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Distribution</td>\n<td>static musl build, <code>cargo-dist</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"milestones\">Milestones</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Ship</th>\n<th>Done when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Walk a directory</td>\n<td>prints every <code>.log</code> file under a path</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Match lines</td>\n<td>prints <code>path:line:text</code> for a regex</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Parallelise</td>\n<td>4 threads, results interleaved correctly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Be fast</td>\n<td><code>--release</code> beats <code>grep -r</code> on 2 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Be usable</td>\n<td><code>--json</code>, <code>--top N</code>, Ctrl-C, exit codes 0/1/2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Be shippable</td>\n<td>one static binary, no glibc dependency</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"crates\">Crates</h2>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\"